{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a4a2d4cb45b05008","name":"Zolghast","source":{"id":"source:reference-a4a2d4cb45b05008","title":"Zolghast","revision":21001,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:58:15Z","sha256":"1dbe3c6317b15784a8e5f652480dbfd454726d75c4eb68a51c26b0b02a107989","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21001","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Zolghast&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a4a2d4cb45b05008","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy at War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_at_War"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["This ",{"tag":"a","children":["Zygerrian"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Zygerrian","referenceId":"reference:234f7196c586c1b9"}," officer stands about as tall as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"},", with dark red hair that almost seems crimson. Bony protrusions jut from the skin of his face, and his features seem angular. Though he appears to be in good shape, his cheeks are somewhat hollow, suggesting that he does not keep himself in excellent health."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Commander Zolghast is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Zygerrian"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Zygerrian","referenceId":"reference:234f7196c586c1b9"},", a native of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Outer Rim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Outer_Rim?action=edit&redlink=1"}," whose Species is known for its violence and combat prowess. Zolghast's paranoia leaves him holed up in his bunker for long periods of time. Since Zolghast is the only one with the firing codes, the heroes will need to subdue him and take the codes from him. If the heroes speak to Zolghast, he adopts the sneering tone of a man who thinks his enemies are beneath his notice. He will not give up the codes willingly, and if he sees a chance to escape out the front of the bunker he does so.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Tactics"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Commander Zolghast's paranoia has prepared him well for the day he always suspected would eventually come when the Republic would send its assassins, which is what he assumes the heroes to be. He uses ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Anticipate Movement"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Anticipate_Movement"}]}," to maneuver his allies into position whenever the heroes try to approach him, trying to use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["B1-Series Battle Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/B1-Series_Battle_Droids"}," and his ",{"tag":"a","children":["Geonosian Bodyguards"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Geonosian_Bodyguards"}," to keep them far enough away that it is difficult for them to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun"}," him. Likewise, he uses ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Deployment Tactics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Deployment_Tactics"}]}," to make sure that his ",{"tag":"a","children":["Geonosian Bodyguards"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Geonosian_Bodyguards"}," have a better chance to hit the heroes with their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Electrostaffs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Electrostaffs"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Zolghast Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Zygerrian"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Zygerrian","referenceId":"reference:234f7196c586c1b9"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.mirahez